      "content": "Even a small dose of benadryl can dangerously amplify the depressant effects of hydrocodone, creating a \"cocktail\" that severely suppresses your breathing and the body's natural ability to wake up for gepf vital functions. Cutting a pill doesn't make it safer; the combined chemical load can still cause life-threatening respiratory failure much faster than anticipated. Please contact your doctor again specifically to ask about safer sleep options, as their advice to \"keep taking the hydro\" implies this interaction is their current concern for you to avoid.",
